// 'Utah Teapot (full)' — Benedikt Bitterli (CC0, public domain;
// crediting the artist encouraged). The full glass teapot of tea on a
// checkered floor under a captured sky — the classic, with media.
// Official pbrt-v4 export from https://benedikt-bitterli.me/resources/
// — `scenes/corpus/fetch.sh teapot-full` materializes the source; this
// RON was bootstrapped once by `cenote-cli import
// sources/bitterli/teapot-full/scene-v4.pbrt` and is the source of
// truth — re-imports diff into scratch, never over it. The octahedral
// PFM sky resamples to the derived, gitignored `teapot-full-sky.exr`
// beside this file (the corpus README has the regeneration recipe).
//
// Import fidelity: two knowing gaps. The tea is a homogeneous
// absorbing medium (MakeNamedMedium/MediumInterface) the renderer
// can't carry until M8 volumes — the pot pours clear glass here, the
// dominant visual divergence from the pbrt reference. And the floor's
// procedural checkerboard texture has no importer support (imports
// mid-gray); curated to the identical 20×20 checker the CI corpus
// baked to a committed PNG (tests/scenes/teapot-full/textures/).
(
    version: 2,
    ops: [
        Settings((
            name: "main",
            resolution: Some((1280, 720)),
            spp: Some(64),
            max_bounces: Some(65),
            seed: None,
        )),
        Camera((
            name: "main",
            position: Some((23.170126, 15.714214, -0.17247628)),
            look_at: Some((22.297527, 15.225801, -0.16757579)),
            up: Some((-0.48840514, 0.8726124, 0.0027428637)),
            vfov_degrees: Some(20.114292),
